{"UFO":{"id":"608b840e-53b4-48b1-91e8-3989d3089775","word":"UFO","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"an unidentified flying object","tags":["masculine"],"word":"óvni"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"an unidentified flying object","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ovni"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"an unidentified flying object","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ufo"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"After the case had been reported in the newspapers, Mrs. Gracindo de Souza, wife of a member of the local stock exchange, told police that she and her daughter had been driving down Alameda Sao Boaventura when they had seen an^([sic]) UFO hovering over the clearing where the bodies were later discovered.","ref":"1967, Brad Steiger, Joan Whritenour, “Someone Up There May Not Like Us”, in Flying Saucers Are Hostile, Tandem Publishing, published 1975, →ISBN, →OCLC, page 13:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[235,238]],"id":"9fbf8e29-e4bb-4685-943a-c89259d54ab0"},{"text":"To my way of thinking, there is every bit as much evidence for the existence of UFOs as there is for the existence of God. Probably far more. At least in the case of UFOs there have been countless taped and filmed—and, by the way, unexplained—sightings from all over the world, along with documented radar evidence seen by experienced military and civilian radar operators.","ref":"2004, George Carlin, “THEY CAME FROM OUT OF THE SKY”, in When Will Jesus Bring the Pork Chops?, New York: Hyperion Books, →ISBN, →OCLC, →OL, page 12:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[80,84],[166,170]],"id":"a0164ff3-b259-40fe-a13c-5e9cb5a6bb11"}],"wikidata":["Q421"],"senseid":["en:Q421"],"attestations":[{"date":"from 20th c.","references":[]}],"categories":["English initialisms","English terms with quotations","en:Ufology"],"links":[["unidentified flying object","unidentified flying object#English:_Q421"],["alien","alien"],["spacecraft","spacecraft"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"UAP"}],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"USO"}],"glosses":["Initialism of unidentified flying object; (loosely) an alien spacecraft."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","initialism"],"alt_of":[{"word":"unidentified flying object","extra":"(loosely) an alien spacecraft"}],"id":"8f97917f-d8a2-4c5e-983a-4862efad94f6"},{"examples":[{"text":"UFOs differ from WIPs in that a WIP is a project one is actively pursuing, while a UFO runs the risk of never getting finished.","ref":"2007, Kerry Wills, The Close-knit Circle: American Knitters Today, page 107:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3],[0,4],[83,86]],"id":"1685faf5-2ca6-44a9-8a63-74c682ad1876"}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 20th c.","references":[]}],"categories":["English colloquialisms","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["knitting","knitting"],["craft","craft"]],"raw_glosses":["(colloquial) An \"unfinished object\" in knitting or other kinds of craft."],"glosses":["An \"unfinished object\" in knitting or other kinds of craft."],"tags":["colloquial"],"id":"25823888-ea24-425b-8606-75077dcb9f10"},{"topics":["astronomy","natural-sciences"],"attestations":[{"date":"2022","references":[]}],"categories":["English initialisms","en:Astronomy"],"links":[["astronomy","astronomy"],["ultrared","ultrared#English"],["flattened","flattened#English"],["object","object#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(astronomy) Initialism of ultrared flattened object."],"glosses":["Initialism of ultrared flattened object."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","initialism"],"alt_of":[{"word":"ultrared flattened object"}],"id":"ec32e021-9a9d-4946-88fa-2159a249e5c9"}],"related":[{"sense":"unidentified flying object","word":"flying saucer"},{"sense":"unidentified flying object","word":"IFO"}],"synonyms":[]},"ufology":{"id":"43b0ad0b-f74a-4211-8bb1-75395c2d5632","word":"ufology","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the study of UFOs","tags":["feminine"],"word":"ufologia"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the study of UFOs","tags":["feminine"],"word":"ovnilogia"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"I'm an expert in my field\nUfology, yes, it's all real\nAncient aliens, it's all true\nI'm an expert just like you","ref":"2016, Neil Cicierega, “Touch-Tone Telephone”, in Spirit Phone, performed by Lemon Demon:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[26,33]],"id":"8929ce3c-2132-4686-9ed9-e48df1d15756"}],"links":[["study","study"],["UFO","UFO"]],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English terms suffixed with -logy","English terms suffixed with -ology","English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Irish translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Macedonian translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Romanian translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Swedish translations","Terms with Turkish translations","en:Ufology"],"glosses":["The study of UFOs."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"8aea776d-cf99-45a8-94d4-d88351c5f369"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"ufologist":{"id":"9dd01b7e-47b6-42d5-a429-77e8048dec9d","word":"ufologist","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"person who studies UFOs","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ufólogo"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Still, something strange was afoot in Rendlesham, and even if the file is unlikely to satisfy either ufologists or debunkers, it suggests that the truth is still out there.","ref":"2002 December 8, Scott Veale, “Word for Word/The Rendlesham File; Let There Be Lights: Britons Get One Less Thing to Worry About”, in The New York Times:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[101,111]],"id":"cdfd618d-61b8-4e1d-a7e2-7720e38ff48f"},{"text":"But fear of abduction never stopped a good ufologist.","ref":"2010, Monte Dwyer, Red in the Centre: Through a Crooked Lens, Monyer Pty Ltd, page 122:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[43,52]],"id":"f7909341-85c7-428e-89e6-c00a1e5fb194"}],"links":[["UFO","UFO"]],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English terms suffixed with -ist","English terms suffixed with -logist","English terms with quotations","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Macedonian translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Turkish translations","en:People","en:Ufology"],"glosses":["A person who studies UFOs."],"id":"ade77157-486b-40b5-b2f2-e48045996f0b"}],"related":[{"word":"ufology"}],"synonyms":[]},"ufological":{"id":"e877e148-1544-41ca-8df7-5065c4b709d0","word":"ufological","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"pertaining to ufology","word":"ufológico"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["ufology","ufology"]],"glosses":["Of or pertaining to ufology."],"categories":["English adjectives","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms suffixed with -ical","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Danish translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Norwegian Bokmål translatio